Article 21
(1) Efforts to prevent violence against women and children shall be carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government coordinated by the regional apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.
(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by:
a. establishing a network in efforts to prevent violence;
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
- 13 -
c. establishing a violence prevention system;
d. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence; and
e. providing critical education on the rights of women and children for the community.

Article 14
(1) Regional Government is obligated and responsible to implement efforts to protect women and children victims of violence through:
a. policy determination;
b. preparation of program and activity planning;
e. establishment of P2TP2A;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure;
e. allocating budget; and
f. establishment of FPKK.
(2) To anticipate the occurrence of acts of violence, the Regional Government provides services for victims in the form of:
a. facilitating the establishment of P2TP2A;
b. facilitating P2TP2A facilities and infrastructure according to capacity; and c. facilitating FPKK as a network forum for victim handling.

Article 9
Neglect as referred to in Article 5 letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of a child properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after a child as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts that neglect a person within the scope of their household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

